## Why This Is Asked
Fresh bit-hack that demonstrates mastery of fixed-step SWAR technique and portability across languages.

## Key Concepts
- SWAR fixed-masks and staged swaps
- Bitwise rotation-free reversal
- Unsigned 32-bit wrap handling in JavaScript/TypeScript

## Code Example
```javascript
function reverseBits32(n) {
  n = ((n >>> 1) & 0x55555555) | ((n & 0x55555555) << 1);
  n = ((n >>> 2) & 0x33333333) | ((n & 0x33333333) << 2);
  n = ((n >>> 4) & 0x0F0F0F0F) | ((n & 0x0F0F0F0F) << 4);
  n = ((n >>> 8) & 0x00FF00FF) | ((n & 0x00FF00FF) << 8);
  n = (n >>> 16) | (n << 16);
  return n >>> 0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for 64-bit integers in languages with 64-bit ops?
- How to verify correctness with quick property tests (e.g., n reversing twice yields n)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason about 128 bit manipulations and zero edge cases without branching.

## Key Concepts
- Branchless bit tricks
- 128 bit layout as hi and lo
- De Bruijn based ctz for 64 and 32 bit values
- Handling zero input gracefully

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;

static inline int ctz64(uint64_t x) {
  if (x == 0) return 64;
  static const int tab[64] = { /* 64 entries */ };
  uint64_t y = x & -x;
  return tab[(y * 0x03f79d71b4cb0a89ULL) >> 58];
}

int lsbIndex128(uint128 x) {
  uint64_t lo = x.lo, hi = x.hi;
  int a = ctz64(lo);
  int b = 64 + ctz64(hi);
  int m = - (int)(lo != 0);
  int res = (a & m) | (b & ~m);
  return (lo | hi) == 0 ? -1 : res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt if 128 bit intrinsics are unavailable
- Extend to msbIndex128 with branchless patterns

## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with bit-slicing and fixed-mask patterns on multi-limb integers, not just 64-bit tricks. It also checks understanding of dividing work across 128-bit by treating halves independently. 

## Key Concepts
- Fixed masks for pairwise swaps (even/odd bits)
- 128-bit represented as two 64-bit lanes
- Branchless, constant-time bit permutation

## Code Example
```javascript
typedef struct { uint64_t hi; uint64_t lo; } uint128;
uint128 swapAdjacentBits128(uint128 x){
  const uint64_t A = 0x5555555555555555ULL; // even bits
  const uint64_t B = 0xAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAULL; // odd bits
  uint128 r;
  r.lo = ((x.lo & A) << 1) | ((x.lo & B) >> 1);
  r.hi = ((x.hi & A) << 1) | ((x.hi & B) >> 1);
  return r;
}
```

